        <mxCell id="e48" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=0;strokeColor=#000000;strokeWidth=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=9;fontColor=#000000;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="sys_localfile" target="sys_sb_decide"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" value="HOW TO READ THIS MAP&#xa;Each row is a role. Each column is a stage, in order from account set-up to monitoring. Arrows show handoffs and the order of steps. Diamonds are decisions. Dashed boxes are external or optional services.&#xa;Endpoint names come from server/src/routes. Role gates come from server/src/middleware/auth.js and lib/authz.js.&#xa;&#xa;ROLE ACCESS (from code)&#xa;Administrator: full access. Receptionist: reservation desk, chat, price requests. Accounting: finance and ledger, refund confirmation, price requests. Operations: housekeeping, kitchen and tours tasks and inventory. Customer: own bookings, orders, pass and reviews.&#xa;Ledger entries and reconcile need administrator or accounting. Backup export, import and clear are administrator only.&#xa;Cancellation: a guest may cancel only pending or confirmed stays. Full refund inside 5 hours of booking, 50% after. Staff cancellations are always full refund.&#xa;&#xa;OBSERVATIONS&#xa;No payment gateway: bookings are confirmed with payment_status unpaid. Refunds move to refund_pending, then accounting or admin confirms.&#xa;The /dev sandbox has no role guard in the client router. Review before production use." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=12;fontSize=12;fontColor=#000000;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="2578" width="1530" height="260" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
